  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 103.60 Total organic carbon (TOC)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 103.60 “Total organic carbon (TOC)” means the sum of the concentrations, in milligrams per liter (mg/L), of all organic carbon, measured using heat, oxygen, ultraviolet irradiation, chemical oxidants, or combinations of these oxidants that convert organic carbon to carbon dioxide, rounded to 2 significant figures.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Dw 100) #10606, eff 6-1-14; renumbered by #10770 (from Env-Dw 103.58); renumbered by #12180 (from Env-Dw 103.59)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw100.html"
